0..73 Comment "/// This source declares an indexed family whose data block writes a rule"
74..149 Comment "/// over its constructors, and one constructor states its index at a field."
150..153 Comment "///"
154..232 Comment "/// It pins the refusal of a constructor rule on such a family. A rule relates"
233..311 Comment "/// two terms at one index, and the checkers read the index of a term where it"
312..326 Comment "/// is closed."
327..330 Comment "///"
331..411 Comment "/// The lowering reads the rules of a family after the description route. A rule"
